staffTitle: Sharing
staffHeading: What appears on <b>other websites</b>
---
{#- SHARING (mockup board 9, "Everything that goes on other websites"; the nav
   name is Chase's — "Other websites" read wrong).

   Six things can appear on somebody else's website: the roadmap, goal
   progress, prayer, videos, the sign-up form and the contact form. They used
   to live on two pages in three layouts, with the colors set in two places.
   Now one page: the six on the left, the real preview in the middle, and on
   the right what decides whether it is live and the code to paste. Colors
   once, at the top, because every one of the six wears them.

   ORGANIZED AS WAYS TO SHARE, so a data feed or notifications later is a new
   row on the left, not a new page.

   THE PREVIEW ALSO STAYS WHERE THE WORDS ARE WRITTEN — Updates opens it
   beside its list. What lives here is what is set once: sharing, colors, code.

   ONE SAVE BAR, like the rest of the console: switching something to Live,
   picking a color, rewording a form are all changes until Save. -#}

<div class="sh-page">

{#- ONE PAIR OF COLORS FOR ALL SIX. The second is matched to the first unless
   somebody picks it; picking it is the whole control. Administrator-only,
   like sharing itself: both change what the public sees. -#}
<div class="sh-colors" id="shColors">
  <span class="sh-lbl" data-i18n="sh.colors">Colors · all six</span>
  <span class="emb-colour">
    <input type="color" id="shAccent" aria-label="Accent color">
    <input type="text" id="shAccentHex" class="emb-hex" maxlength="7" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Accent color hex">
  </span>
  <span class="emb-colour">
    <input type="color" id="shAccent2" aria-label="Second color">
    <span class="sh-pair" id="shPairNote"></span>
    <button type="button" class="link-btn" id="shPairAuto" data-i18n="sh.matchAgain" hidden>Match automatically</button>
  </span>
  <span class="c-gap"></span>
  <label class="sh-pick"><span data-i18n="emb.theme">Background</span>
    <select id="shTheme">
      <option value="auto" data-i18n="emb.auto">Match their page</option>
      <option value="light" data-i18n="emb.light">Always light</option>
      <option value="dark" data-i18n="emb.dark">Always dark</option>
    </select>
  </label>
</div>

<div class="sh-grid">
  <nav class="sh-list" id="shList" aria-label="What is shared"></nav>

  <div class="sh-mid">
    <div class="emb-stagebar">
      <div class="emb-devices" role="tablist" aria-label="Width">
        <button type="button" class="emb-device is-on" role="tab" aria-selected="true"
                data-width="wide" data-i18n="emb.desktop">Desktop</button>
        <button type="button" class="emb-device" role="tab" aria-selected="false"
                data-width="narrow" data-i18n="emb.mobile">Mobile</button>
      </div>
      <span class="emb-scale-note" id="shScaleNote"></span>
      <span class="c-gap"></span>
      <label class="sh-pick" id="shLangWrap"><span data-i18n="emb.lang">Language</span>
        <select id="shLang"></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="emb-stage" id="shStage">
      <div class="emb-scale" id="shScale">
        <iframe id="shFrame" title="Preview" sandbox="allow-scripts"></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>

    {#- The words a form carries, in every language — "Writing X beside Y",
       as on Updates and Website › Pages. A language left empty shows the
       form's translated defaults. The four widgets have none of their own:
       their words are the ministry's updates, written on Updates. -#}
    <div class="sh-card sh-words" id="shWords" hidden>
      <span class="sh-lbl" data-i18n="sh.words">The words on it</span>
      <div class="ms-writing">
        <label class="ms-pick"><span data-i18n="con.writing">Writing</span>
          <select id="shWriting" class="lang-pick"></select></label>
        <label class="ms-pick" id="shBesideWrap"><span data-i18n="con.beside">beside</span>
          <select id="shBeside" class="lang-pick"></select></label>
      </div>
      <div class="sh-word-fields" id="shWordFields"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="sh-side">
    {#- WHOSE FORMS: Thauma's own, or this ministry's. Only for accounts that can
       reach Thauma's (the Mailing page's rule), and it only changes the two forms:
       the four widgets are a ministry's data. -#}
    <div class="ml-whose sh-card" id="shScope" hidden>
      <span class="ml-whose-label" data-i18n="ml.scope">Whose lists</span>
      <div class="ml-whose-opts">
        <button type="button" class="ml-whose-opt is-on" data-scope="partner" id="shScopeMine"></button>
        <button type="button" class="ml-whose-opt" data-scope="organization" data-i18n="ml.scopeOrg">Thauma</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sh-card sh-live" id="shLiveCard">
      <button type="button" class="switch" id="shLive" role="switch" aria-checked="false">
        <span class="switch-track"><span class="switch-state">Off</span><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
        <span class="switch-label"><span data-i18n="sh.live">Live</span></span>
      </button>
      <p class="rolegate" id="shAdminOnly" hidden data-i18n="emb.adminOnly">An administrator changes this.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="sh-card" id="shListsCard" hidden>
      <span class="sh-lbl" data-i18n="sh.lists">Lists on this form</span>
      <div class="sh-switches" id="shLists"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sh-card" id="shContactCard" hidden>
      <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="ml.ctTo">Send messages to</span>
        <input type="email" id="shCtTo" maxlength="200" placeholder="you@example.org"></label>
      <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="ml.ctFrom">Sent from</span>
        <select id="shCtFrom"></select></label>
      <div class="ct-topics">
        <span class="sh-lbl" data-i18n="ml.ctTopics">What is this about</span>
        <div id="shTopics"></div>
        <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="shAddTopic" data-i18n="ml.ctAddTopic">Add a reason</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sh-card" id="shPeriodCard" hidden>
      <span class="sh-lbl" data-i18n="emb.periodTitle">The period this covers</span>
      <div class="sh-period">
        <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="emb.periodStart">Starts</span><input type="date" id="shStart"></label>
        <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="emb.periodEnd">Ends</span><input type="date" id="shEnd"></label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sh-card">
      <span class="sh-lbl" data-i18n="sh.code">Code to paste</span>
      <pre class="emb-code" id="shCode"></pre>
      <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="shCopy" data-i18n="common.copy">Copy</button>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

{#- FOR DEVELOPERS: the raw data behind the widgets and the guide to it, for
   somebody building their own design. -#}
<details class="sh-card sh-dev" id="shDev">
  <summary><span class="sh-lbl" data-i18n="sh.dev">For developers</span></summary>
  <div class="sh-dev-body">
    <span class="sh-lbl" data-i18n="emb.apiTitle">The data behind it</span>
    <pre class="emb-code" id="shApi"></pre>
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="shCopyApi" data-i18n="common.copy">Copy</button>
    <a class="emb-guide" id="shGuide" download><span data-i18n="emb.guide">Download the developer guide</span></a>
  </div>
</details>

</div>

<div class="ms-savebar" id="shBar" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
  <span class="ms-dirty-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span id="shCount"></span>
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="shDiscard" data-i18n="ms.discard">Discard</button>
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="shSave" data-i18n="sh.save">Save changes</button>
</div>
